  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xをおごる (to treat someone to X)\n- おごってもらう (to be treated by someone)\n- おごってあげる (to treat someone - giving perspective)\n- おごってくれる (to treat someone - receiving perspective)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {割|わ}り{勘|かん} (splitting the bill - opposite concept)\n- ご{馳走|ちそう}する (to treat - more formal)\n- {払|はら}ってあげる (to pay for someone)\n\nINFORMAL KANJI:\nSometimes written as {奢|おご}る, but hiragana is more common.\n\nUSAGE:\nDifferent from {驕|おご}る (to be arrogant), which is a separate word with a different meaning.",
